{"id": "EUVD-2026-59223", "enisaUuid": "3f6f3f78-a803-31b2-a8ab-a91c8a9c71e7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngpio: mvebu: free generic chips on unbind\n\nirq_alloc_domain_generic_chips() allocates generic chip data that must\nbe freed via irq_domain_remove_generic_chips(). The devres action\nmvebu_gpio_remove_irq_domain() only called irq_domain_remove(), which\nonly frees the generic chips if IRQ_DOMAIN_FLAG_DESTROY_GC is set.\nCall irq_domain_remove_generic_chips() explicitly before\nirq_domain_remove() instead.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:55:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:34", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db2b40dc12cd6ae4704f52d62c0147ef31527f60", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3649b04f86b95243fa0c845695051455fa2ba40b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3bfcce441c552133adeeb99c294d0ce8a62612ef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d73e4d790db611da7439e78a6ab6cb32e7885ab8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b11c513ad943f35cf5e8007d3a56279c79b7ed4b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f4rp-fvp9-gmx9", "CVE-2026-72324"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1248b36c-e84f-3dfc-9a42-b18b646ccf57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "812d47889a8e418d7bea9bec383581a34c19183e <d73e4d790db611da7439e78a6ab6cb32e7885ab8"}, {"id": "15fc2d0e-b28e-3cb8-9f75-98818e776198", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "812d47889a8e418d7bea9bec383581a34c19183e <3bfcce441c552133adeeb99c294d0ce8a62612ef"}, {"id": "16521c4b-c86f-3c15-a4ec-d1b2c3c40ee1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "812d47889a8e418d7bea9bec383581a34c19183e <b11c513ad943f35cf5e8007d3a56279c79b7ed4b"}, {"id": "26044bb8-5b6b-3d4e-9426-a3e45b32087a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.8.9 <4.9"}, {"id": "27950a3e-039a-3177-9537-6ff7fe2a1513",